course: dictionary
lesson: 15997
title: Vaccinated and protected
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Vaccinated is an adjective, and it is also the past tense of the verb vaccinate. To be vaccinated means to be given a vaccine, a medicine that teaches your body to fight a disease before you catch it.
explain: Vaccines are usually given by an injection. «Sam was vaccinated against measles before he started school.» The word before is a clue: the vaccine came first, so Sam's body was ready if it ever met the disease.
explain: Look for clues in the words around vaccinated. The word against tells you what the vaccine protects you from. «Ask the nurse if you are fully vaccinated» means you should check that you have had all the vaccines you need.
fact: Vaccinated means given a vaccine, a medicine that protects you from a disease.
fact: «Vaccinated» is the past tense of the verb vaccinate.
fact: Vaccines help protect you and the people around you from diseases like measles, polio and flu.
fact: Pets can be vaccinated too, to keep them safe from illness.
fact: Useful phrases: get vaccinated, fully vaccinated, vaccinated against.
exercise: «Sam was vaccinated against measles before he started school.» What does vaccinated mean here? | Measured for new clothes | Taken to school by car | Had a bad cold | *Given a vaccine to protect against a disease
exercise: A vaccine is best described as | A kind of school bag | *A medicine that teaches the body to fight a disease | A game played at school | A type of sweet
exercise: «Ask the nurse if you are fully vaccinated.» Find and copy the word that means given a medicine to protect you from a disease. | fully | ask | *vaccinated | nurse
test: Why does a vaccine protect you before you catch a disease? | Because it keeps you off school | Because it makes you sneeze | Because it cures you once you are already ill | *Because it teaches your body to fight the disease before you catch it
test: Which word is the past tense of vaccinate? | vaccine | vaccinates | vaccinating | *vaccinated
exam: What can being vaccinated protect you and other people from? | Hunger and thirst | Bad weather and wet days | *Diseases like measles, polio and flu | Lost toys and muddy shoes
